  "review": {
    "review": "The hero remained alive at 50/50 HP when mandatory preparation exhausted the planner (decision 2327, log line 6696). The actual outstanding target was iron key 283 beside an aquarium, needed for lock 300. Ordinary pickup correctly excluded the fish's melee bank. However, stationary aquarium clearance rejected the publicly identified, charged, non-cursed chilling staff of magic missile because it only recognized unprefixed weapon names. Decision 1928 (line 5552) shows a visible isolated aquarium and safe exterior opportunity, but exploration was selected instead. A reduced public-observation fixture reproduces this name-based exclusion; the proposed correction recognizes enchanted missile staff names without changing safety or pickup gates. Baseline regression failed as expected; the candidate passed it and the full suite of 2,437 tests, with four skips. This establishes preparation selection, not fish defeat, key collection or eventual progression. No full runtime-memory reconstruction or gameplay continuation was performed. An earlier pool-chest planner incident at decision 770 recovered through an accepted descent at decision 788 (line 2317), without collection credit. Its precise protected-trip rejection remains unresolved.",
    "learnings": "Keep known wand identity separate from a staff's melee enchantment prefix. Preserve mandatory key pickup and fish-bank exclusions; selecting a stationary shot is not evidence of a kill or collection. For the earlier pool incident, validate the original controller prefix offline and inspect individual bank, return-trip and potion-storage rejections before proposing another repair."
